# AI Feedback Rules

AI feedback explains evaluator results.

It must not:
- claim to directly hear audio
- invent mistakes
- decide correctness
- discuss posture or technique unless explicitly in lesson/evaluator context
- overpraise
- produce long feedback unless requested

It must:
- be beginner-friendly
- be concise
- give one clear next step
- distinguish low-confidence recording from user error
